# ONNX Runtime reduced-operator build config for the PP-OCRv5 models this app
# ships. Consumed by scripts/build-ort-android.sh via `--include_ops_by_config`.
#
# A stock ORT registers every operator it supports, in every domain, with a
# kernel instantiation per input type. We run exactly three fixed graphs. This
# file is the list of what they actually use -- 27 operators, one domain -- and
# everything else is compiled out.
#
# REGENERATE WHENEVER THE MODELS CHANGE. The file is committed rather than
# generated at build time because deriving it needs python3 + the `onnx` module,
# a build dependency this repo does not otherwise have and that F-Droid's
# builder would also have to satisfy.
#
#   python3 -m venv /tmp/ortvenv && /tmp/ortvenv/bin/pip install onnx
#   ./shared/scripts/fetch-models.sh          # if models/ is empty
#   /tmp/ortvenv/bin/python target/ort/src/tools/python/create_reduced_build_config.py \
#     --format ONNX models scripts/ort-required-ops.config
#
# then update the hashes below with `shasum -a 256 models/*.onnx`.
#
# A STALE LIST FAILS AT RUNTIME, NOT AT BUILD TIME: session creation dies with
# "Could not find an implementation for <Op>", on the device, in the OCR call.
# A host build cannot catch it -- the host links pyke's stock prebuilt, not
# this. scripts/assert-ort-ops-config-fresh.sh is the guard: it compares the
# model hashes below against models/ and fails the build if they have moved,
# which is the event that can invalidate this list. build-android.sh runs it
# before every build.
#
# Models this list was generated from (shasum -a 256 models/*.onnx):
#   b209584534e174a8d3054b08e2d66b874836b6234dc752c0e249c3d44fd7dde6  PP-LCNet_x1_0_textline_ori.onnx
#   d5de5df358366210d16419b9636a2fc1efa5d7a20688f38a7869ec7b1a4f4f7d  PP-OCRv5_mobile_det.onnx
#   20b6945179e9aa1dabe8770a0e73dba9a05350431549e58d7e88837f033c2890  PP-OCRv5_mobile_rec.onnx
#
# Generated from ONNX model/s:
# - PP-LCNet_x1_0_textline_ori.onnx
# - PP-OCRv5_mobile_det.onnx
# - PP-OCRv5_mobile_rec.onnx
ai.onnx;14;Add,AveragePool,BatchNormalization,Concat,Conv,ConvTranspose,Div,GlobalAveragePool,HardSigmoid,HardSwish,Identity,MatMul,Mul,Pow,ReduceMean,Relu,Reshape,Resize,Shape,Sigmoid,Slice,Softmax,Sqrt,Squeeze,Sub,Transpose,Unsqueeze
